Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:19:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Give the wireDemo hierarchy nine OPAQUE flatten boundaries

Clash's cleanupGraph inlines every non-OPAQUE binder into its caller and
re-runs the flatten strategy on the result, so a call chain rewrites the
same expression once per level: core (68k terms) -> bringUp (114k) ->
demoTest_mkUserCore1 (114k) -> wireDemoTest (113k). Those four nodes were
8.2s of the 18.5s that flattening took. An OPAQUE binder is a boundary
that flattenNode does not cross.

The nine pragmas cut flattening from 18.4s to 9.7s and wireDemoTest from
1m06s to 59.3s, at eight capabilities on a machine where the run-to-run
spread is about 2s.

The HDL is re-partitioned, not changed: 70 modules become 79, the
top-level port list is byte-identical, and the design keeps its 2834 reg
declarations, 2043 always blocks and 196 blackbox instantiations.
